# Project contract

- This is a Windows-only WPF editor for GTA III and GTA Vice City text resources. Target `.NET 10` (`net10.0-windows`), C# 14, nullable reference types, SDK analyzers, CommunityToolkit.Mvvm, and MSTest/Microsoft Testing Platform.
- Treat `README.md`, `GTA GXT Editor.csproj`, `global.json`, `.editorconfig`, and nearby tests as the source of truth. Inspect the affected implementation and tests before editing; keep changes narrow and preserve unrelated work.
- Respect the existing layers: `Views`/`Themes` render WPF UI, `ViewModels` own presentation state and commands, `Services` perform workflows/I/O/validation, `Models` hold data, and `GTAIII`/`GTAVC` implement game-specific binary behavior through `Contracts/CommonGXTManager`.
- Never edit `bin/`, `obj/`, or pinned third-party files under `Tools/InnoSetup/`. Do not hand-edit the large canonical encounter metadata; use `scripts/generate-vice-city-encounter-metadata.ps1` and verify its tests. Change bundled mappings/reference assets only when the task explicitly changes their contract.
- Follow `.editorconfig`: UTF-8, CRLF, final newline, four spaces for C#/XAML, sorted `System` usings, and preferably file-scoped namespaces. Preserve intentional legacy namespace/API compatibility instead of performing drive-by renames.
- Add or update automated tests for behavior changes. Keep English and Belarusian UI resources and paired documentation (`README*.md`, `docs/*.md` plus `*.be.md`) synchronized when user-visible behavior changes.

# Verification

- Build with `dotnet build "GTA GXT Editor.slnx" --configuration Release`.
- Run focused tests while iterating with `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/run-tests.ps1 -Configuration Release -Filter <filter>`.
- Before handoff, run the full suite with `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/run-tests.ps1 -Configuration Release`. If verification cannot run, report the exact command and reason; never claim success without running it.
